            {
              "@id": "http://smart.who.int/base/skill/smart-guideline-end-to-end",
              "@type": "bootstrap:Skill",
              "ambiguous": false,
              "description": "The whole road from a use case to a running application on WHO SMART Guidelines, for a new guideline or a jurisdiction's adaptation, as an orchestrator of ten named stage skills, each with its own input and output contract: guideline-use-case, dak-l1-library, recommendation-extraction, l2-dependency-choice, l2-dak-authoring, l3-dependency-choice, l3-fhir-authoring, l4-application-brief, wireframe-design-review and l4-application-build. Each stage's output is the next stage's input. Human adjudication follows every stage as QA, not as a gate, but the order of the stages is a rule: no L3 asset before the L1 extraction and L2 assets it derives from exist with their review requested. Read before starting any end-to-end authoring or adaptation, and to find which skill runs each stage. A request to adapt a WHO guideline, DAK or IG to a country or programme (\"adapt the immunization guidelines to Uganda using these schedules\") is this process, even when it reads like an IG or coding task.",
              "hasIOContract": true,
              "hasInstructions": true,
              "inSubgraph": "http://smart.who.int/base/directory/smart-base-skills",
              "inputSchema": "http://smart.who.int/base/schema/skills/smart-guideline-end-to-end/input.schema.json",
